  <bioghist id="aspace_586d73b38ad89fc1b6dc4b35680f1ef9">
    <head>Biography/History</head>
<p>Donald Carl Eugster is a composer, lyriciststs, and arranger for musicals and the theater. Eugster was born in Hollywood, California on April 14, 1925. Eugster played piano and French horn in the United States Navy band while he served from 1943-1946. Eugster scored his first musical, <title render="italic">Alice in Wonderland</title>, during his undergraduate education at UCLA. Eugster currently lives in Los Angeles and continues to compose and perform across a variety of genres.</p>  </bioghist>
  <bioghist id="aspace_e15cff3d4de9853843da78bd46dbfcbd">
    <head>Alternate Biography/History</head>
<p>Donald Carl Eugster was born in Hollywood, California on April 14, 1925. He earned a B.A. in music composition from California State University, Los Angeles (1948) and studied composition at the University of Southern California for two years with Ernst Toch. He served in US Navy (1943-1946) and played in Navy bands. Over the course of his career he has composed, arranged, and wrote lyrics for a variety of local shows as well as recordings, and a small number of films.  Early in his career he began playing, arranging and conducting for dance bands and musicals, and composing with local theatres in the Los Angeles area. Eugster's first complete score, <title render="italic">Alice  In Wonderland</title>, was produced at UCLA).  Among his many credits are the films <title render="italic">Dragstrip Riot</title> (1958), <title render="italic">The Third Eye</title> (1970), and <title render="italic">Rivals</title> (1972); the recordings <title render="italic">I Forget the Time</title> and <title render="italic">Midnight on a Rainy Monday</title>, both featuring Frankie Laine; and musicals. His professional affiliations have included The American Society of Composers, Authors and Publishers (ASCAP) and Dramatists Guild.</p>  </bioghist>
  <scopecontent id="aspace_a11375b381eaa4324abf0a365661d5c6">
    <head>Scope and Content</head>
<p>The collection contains compositions from his career including music from <title render="italic">Alice in Wonderland</title>, <title render="italic">A Christmas Carol</title>, and<title render="italic"> Hurly Burly</title>. This collection also contains photos, correspondence, and recordings from Eugster's professional life.</p>  </scopecontent>
